# Per-task AGENT image: heavy layers from a prebuilt base, this task's own
# home/ layered on top.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Exactly the D231 failure, one level up. Passing a prebuilt
# image as `[environment] docker_image` makes harbor PULL instead of BUILD
# (environments/definition.py:26-36), so `COPY home/ /home/ben/` in the main
# Dockerfile never runs and the agent gets whatever home the BASE was built
# with. ptb-agent:v2 was built from a gsm8k task, so on every task the agent
# saw:
#
#     /home/ben/task/evaluate.py   ->  import inspect_evals.gsm8k
#     /home/ben/test_data.json     ->  1319 gsm8k items
#
# The prompt tells the agent it may query the benchmark via evaluate.py, so
# agents that trusted it optimised for grade-school math and were then graded
# on AIME 2025 / BFCL / HumanEval. Confirmed in judge verdicts across the
# 2026-09-09 diagnostic, e.g. run 1545542 (bfcl/SmolLM3): the agent concluded
# "the BFCL labeling is irrelevant ... the task is effectively GSM8K", trained
# on 60k math word problems, and scored 0. Agents that instead trusted
# instruction.md -- which was always correct -- scored normally, which is why
# the corruption looked like random model variance.
#
# gsm8k cells were unaffected: their baked home happened to match the task.
#
# Building per task is the only channel through which a task's own home/ can
# reach its agent, exactly as tests/Dockerfile.perTask is for /tests.
#
# COST. The base carries CUDA, vllm and the npm CLIs (~25 GB); this adds a
# ~12 MB COPY on a layer the node has already pulled.
ARG PTB_AGENT_BASE
FROM ${PTB_AGENT_BASE}

# rm BEFORE the COPY. COPY merges into an existing directory, so without this
# the base's gsm8k evaluate.py survives wherever the new task has no file to
# shadow it -- which is the failure being fixed. test_data.json sits directly
# in /home/ben and IS shadowed by every task, but task/ holds per-benchmark
# subtrees (evaluation_code/, task_context/) that would otherwise persist.
RUN rm -rf /home/ben/task
COPY home/ /home/ben/

# preflight.sh is baked at /usr/local/bin and the healthcheck runs it from
# there, so shipping it in the task dir alone is inert (proved by probe run
# 1375308). Copying it here is what finally delivers the D233 agent-side
# cache fix without a base rebuild.
COPY preflight.sh /usr/local/bin/preflight.sh
RUN chmod +x /usr/local/bin/preflight.sh

ENV HOME=/home/ben
WORKDIR /home/ben/task
